# Umbrella Navigation

This project is an Elixir umbrella with all domain apps under `apps/`. The dependency direction is strictly enforced: Core never depends on Peripheral, Plugins, or API. Peripheral never depends on API. Plugins depend on Core and on `api_facade` only. API may depend on Core, Peripheral, and API, and nothing depends on `api_web`. `api_web` and `peripheral_telemetry` may depend on `engine_plugins`.

## App Directory Map

| App | Domain | Directory | Purpose |
|-----|--------|-----------|---------|
| `core_types` | Core | `apps/core_types/` | Behaviour-free structs, shared types (`Identity`, `Token`, event payloads) |
| `core_execution` | Core | `apps/core_execution/` | PI/FNI runtime, resume, payload cap |
| `core_events` | Core | `apps/core_events/` | EngineEventBus, pending sweeper |
| `core_timers` | Core | `apps/core_timers/` | ISO 8601 scheduler |
| `core_expressions` | Core | `apps/core_expressions/` | FEEL evaluator |
| `core_bpmn` | Core | `apps/core_bpmn/` | XML parser, ModelCache, linter gate |
| `peripheral_persistence` | Peripheral | `apps/peripheral_persistence/` | Ash + AshPostgres, Mix `bfw.retention.purge` |
| `peripheral_telemetry` | Peripheral | `apps/peripheral_telemetry/` | :telemetry counters, /stats |
| `engine_plugins` | Plugins | `apps/engine_plugins/` | Plugin registry, in-BEAM loader |
| `api_auth` | API | `apps/api_auth/` | JWT validation |
| `api_facade` | API | `apps/api_facade/` | `BfwEngine.Api` service-layer facade |
| `api_web` | API | `apps/api_web/` | REST + GraphQL + WebSocket + Admin |

## Key Rules

- **Mix commands** run from the project root: `mix compile`, `mix test`, `mix credo --strict`
- **Single-app tests**: `mix test apps/core_execution/test`
- **Single-app compile**: `mix compile` still compiles all apps (umbrella behavior); use the full suite
- **Dependency direction**: Core apps may depend on `core_types` and each other within Core. Peripheral apps may depend on Core and on each other. Plugins (`engine_plugins`) may depend on Core and on `api_facade`. API apps may depend on Core, Peripheral, and API. Nothing depends on `api_web`. The explicit extra edges are `api_web` → `engine_plugins` and `peripheral_telemetry` → `engine_plugins`. `apps/api_web/test/architecture/dependency_direction_test.exs` enforces this graph.
- **`BfwEngine.Api`** lives in its own module (not an app); it is the Ash Code Interface shared by all API apps and plugins
- **Documentation** lives in `docs/` at the project root, not inside individual apps
- **Configuration** lives in `config/` at the project root (`config.exs`, `runtime.exs`)
